## Subagent usage instructions

If you've reached the maximum number of REPL iterations, spawn a sub-agent to finish the task:
<repl_input lang="python">
subagent_inputs = __inputs__  # The task's inputs. IMPORTANT: YOU MUST INCLUDE __inputs__ IN THE SUBAGENT INPUTS
subagent_inputs["prev_repl_history"] = prev_repl_history + __repl_history__  # Your REPL history (if prev_repl_history exists)
# subagent_inputs["prev_repl_history"] = __repl_history__  # Your REPL history (if prev_repl_history doesn't exist)
subagent_inputs["prev_progress_summary"] = ...  # Summary of progress made so far
...  # Add any other state that you're tracking
RETURN jaz.invoke(__task__, return_type=__return_type__, **subagent_inputs)
</repl_input>

If a variable you need to observe is too large and truncated, analyze it by iterating over it
and calling subagents on each chunk:
<repl_input lang="python">
analysis = ...
for chunk in ...:
    subagent_result = jaz.invoke(
        ...,  # Instructions for the subagent to analyze the chunk
        return_type=__return_type__,
        chunk=chunk,  # Or some other variable name
    )
    ...  # Accumulate subagent_result into analysis
</repl_input>
